2. WHY A RE-SHOOT CANNOT BE THE RECEIPT
   The producer launches start_all.py, drives Edge, screenshots and then writes
   the gallery. A second shoot carries a new clock stamp and new PNG bytes by
   construction, so byte equality can never hold. The reproducible half is the
   page: gallery(report) + the shipped post-render channel.

3. READ-ONLY PROBE (system temp only, nothing written into the repo)
   Replaying the landed report through the producer's own gallery() and FACES
   table, then applying face_backhop.inject_text, produced a 6450B page whose
   line diff against the landed page was ONE line: the image src
       landed: src='live/hub.png'
       replay: src='../../../../Desktop/.../preview/live/hub.png'
   The gallery derives the relative path from os.path.dirname(path), so the
   gap is positional - a function of where the page is written, not of the
   derivation.

4. SEAM ADDED AT THE SOURCE
   tools/ceo_live_shot.py: gallery(rows, report, path, proof=None, page_dir=None)
   page_dir is where the page BELIEVES it sits; it defaults to where the bytes
   go, so a no-argument run is byte-identical to before (checked by reading the
   landed pair back through the receipt).

